{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3f9c1a2e-0b7a-4d1e-9c3a-6b2f8d4a1c07",
    "name": "NeoAssets Scraping API",
    "description": "Public scraping API of NeoAssets.\n\nSetup:\n1. Import also the environment `neoassets-scraping.postman_environment.json` and select it.\n2. Set `clientId` and `clientSecret` with your developer app credentials.\n3. Set `systemId` (from GET /scrape/systems, e.g. `snes`) and `searchName` (e.g. `mario`).\n4. To test as a registered user, set `userApiKey` with a personal API key (Profile page). Leave it empty for guest mode.\n5. Run the requests in order. `Games - by name` stores `romHash`/`romHashParam` so the by-hash requests work.\n\n`GET /scrape/games` requires `system_id`, `family` or `group` plus a ROM hash or a name, and returns a SINGLE game (`game`, null when nothing matched) with `matched_by` (`hash`|`name`) and the game's `scrapes` counter.\n\nRate limit tests: the two `Rate Limit - *` requests loop themselves via `pm.execution.setNextRequest`, so they MUST be run with the Collection Runner (not the Send button). They stop as soon as a 429 is observed.\n\nSystem Art Packs: `GET /packs` lists approved packs (sorted by downloads, paginated); `GET /packs/{packId}` returns the full install payload and bumps the download counter; `Contribute - create submission` creates a pending contribution to an approved pack (set `packId`, `packName`, `packAuthor` and `userToken`).\n\nRate limiting: the pack download endpoint (`/packs/{packId}/download`) is limited per (IP, pack) to ~4 req/min per pack, so the download counter reflects real installs and cannot be flooded.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
